1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,881
Ten thousand Cents.

2
00:00:02,484 --> 00:00:05,700
The number of Sets that can exist at any given time

3
00:00:05,746 --> 00:00:09,323
is capped by the scarcest Cent the Set requires.

4
00:00:10,627 --> 00:00:13,343
A Patina Set needs a notable desert,

5
00:00:13,378 --> 00:00:16,373
and 598 Cents carry one.

6
00:00:17,283 --> 00:00:21,138
A Sig Set needs a significant desert: 150.

7
00:00:21,864 --> 00:00:24,963
A Spectrum Set needs a gold: 69.

8
00:00:25,689 --> 00:00:29,056
A Fulls Set needs a full verdigris: 15.

9
00:00:29,699 --> 00:00:33,170
A Full Spectrum Set needs a full gold: 9.

10
00:00:33,954 --> 00:00:37,670
A Full Contamination Set needs scotch tape: 7.

11
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:44,216
And the 1940s Set needs the only Cent dated 1949: 1.

12
00:00:45,658 --> 00:00:48,165
One Cent, and one collector at a time.

13
00:00:49,348 --> 00:00:51,508
Every time a Cent changes hands,

14
00:00:51,636 --> 00:00:54,479
it can complete one Set and break another.
